    "content": "〔卷一・甲部(2)〕（5 分）\n\n兩個相似的圓錐，其高之比為 $2:3$。\n(a) 若較小的圓錐的體積為 $40\\text{ cm}^{3}$，求較大的圓錐的體積。（3 分）\n(b) 若較大的圓錐的總表面積為 $90\\text{ cm}^{2}$，求較小的圓錐的總表面積。（2 分）",
    "explanation": "相似立體只有三條比：長度 $k$、面積 $k^{2}$、體積 $k^{3}$。本題刻意把 (a) 設為「由小求大」而 (b) 設為「由大求小」，就是要檢驗考生有沒有留意乘與除的方向 —— 兩問若都按同一方向計算，其中一問必錯。做這類題時，先寫下比的方向（誰是 2、誰是 3），再代數字，可避免大部分失分。",
    "referenceAnswer": "(a) $135\\text{ cm}^{3}$\n(b) $40\\text{ cm}^{2}$",
    "marks": 5,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) $135\\text{ cm}^{3}$\n(b) $40\\text{ cm}^{2}$",
    "contentEn": "[Paper 1 · Section A(2)] (5 marks)\n\nTwo similar cones have heights in the ratio $2:3$.\n(a) If the volume of the smaller cone is $40\\text{ cm}^{3}$, find the volume of the larger cone. (3 marks)\n(b) If the total surface area of the larger cone is $90\\text{ cm}^{2}$, find the total surface area of the smaller cone. (2 marks)",
    "explanationEn": "Similar solids involve only three ratios: length $k$, area $k^{2}$ and volume $k^{3}$. Part (a) deliberately goes from small to large and part (b) from large to small, to test whether candidates notice the direction of multiplication and division. If both parts are computed in the same direction, one of them must be wrong. Writing down the direction of the ratio first, that is, which quantity is the 2 and which the 3, before substituting numbers, prevents most of the marks lost here.",
    "markingScheme": "(a) 相似立體的體積比等於長度比的立方：$V_{1}:V_{2}=2^{3}:3^{3}=8:27$ …… 1 分\n　　$\\dfrac{40}{V_{2}}=\\dfrac{8}{27}$ …… 1 分\n　　$V_{2}=40\\times\\dfrac{27}{8}=135\\text{ cm}^{3}$ …… 1 分\n(b) 相似立體的面積比等於長度比的平方：$A_{1}:A_{2}=2^{2}:3^{2}=4:9$ …… 1 分\n　　$A_{1}=90\\times\\dfrac{4}{9}=40\\text{ cm}^{2}$ …… 1 分",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) For similar solids the ratio of volumes is the cube of the ratio of lengths: $V_{1}:V_{2}=2^{3}:3^{3}=8:27$ …… 1 mark\n    $\\dfrac{40}{V_{2}}=\\dfrac{8}{27}$ …… 1 mark\n    $V_{2}=40\\times\\dfrac{27}{8}=135\\text{ cm}^{3}$ …… 1 mark\n(b) For similar solids the ratio of areas is the square of the ratio of lengths: $A_{1}:A_{2}=2^{2}:3^{2}=4:9$ …… 1 mark\n    $A_{1}=90\\times\\dfrac{4}{9}=40\\text{ cm}^{2}$ …… 1 mark",
    "suggestedMinutes": 6
