    "content": "〔卷一・甲部(2)〕（7 分）\n\n在 $\\triangle ABC$ 中，$AB=8\\text{ cm}$，$AC=5\\text{ cm}$，且 $\\angle BAC=60^{\\circ}$。\n(a) 求 $BC$。（3 分）\n(b) 求 $\\triangle ABC$ 的面積，答案以根式表示。（2 分）\n(c) 求由 $A$ 至 $BC$ 的距離，答案準確至三位有效數字。（2 分）",
    "explanation": "(c) 是本題的關鍵設計：求點到直線的距離，不必另作垂線再解三角形 —— 同一個三角形的面積可以用兩條不同的底與高去表達，於是 (b) 的結果直接成為 (c) 的方程。這種「以面積為橋樑」的做法，在卷一極常出現，值得建立為習慣。另須留意 (b) 要求根式而 (c) 要求三位有效數字：中途保留根式再在最後一步才取近似值，可避免累積誤差。",
    "referenceAnswer": "(a) $BC=7\\text{ cm}$\n(b) 面積 $=10\\sqrt{3}\\text{ cm}^{2}$\n(c) 約 $4.95\\text{ cm}$",
    "marks": 7,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) $BC=7\\text{ cm}$\n(b) Area $=10\\sqrt{3}\\text{ cm}^{2}$\n(c) About $4.95\\text{ cm}$",
    "contentEn": "[Paper 1 · Section A(2)] (7 marks)\n\nIn $\\triangle ABC$, $AB=8\\text{ cm}$, $AC=5\\text{ cm}$ and $\\angle BAC=60^{\\circ}$.\n(a) Find $BC$. (3 marks)\n(b) Find the area of $\\triangle ABC$, giving your answer in surd form. (2 marks)\n(c) Find the distance from $A$ to $BC$, correct to 3 significant figures. (2 marks)",
    "explanationEn": "Part (c) is the designed point of this question: to find the distance from a point to a line there is no need to construct a perpendicular and solve another triangle, because the area of one triangle can be expressed using two different bases and heights, so the result of (b) becomes the equation for (c) directly. This use of area as a bridge appears very often in Paper 1 and is worth making a habit. Note also that (b) asks for surd form while (c) asks for 3 significant figures: keeping the surd through the working and approximating only at the last step avoids accumulated rounding error.",
    "markingScheme": "(a) 由餘弦定理：$BC^{2}=AB^{2}+AC^{2}-2(AB)(AC)\\cos\\angle BAC$ …… 1 分\n　　$=8^{2}+5^{2}-2(8)(5)\\cos 60^{\\circ}=64+25-40=49$ …… 1 分\n　　$BC=7\\text{ cm}$ …… 1 分\n(b) 面積 $=\\dfrac{1}{2}(AB)(AC)\\sin\\angle BAC=\\dfrac{1}{2}(8)(5)\\sin 60^{\\circ}$ …… 1 分\n　　$=20\\times\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=10\\sqrt{3}\\text{ cm}^{2}$ …… 1 分\n(c) 設所求距離為 $h$。以 $BC$ 為底：$\\dfrac{1}{2}(7)h=10\\sqrt{3}$ …… 1 分\n　　$h=\\dfrac{20\\sqrt{3}}{7}\\approx 4.95\\text{ cm}$ …… 1 分",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) By the cosine formula: $BC^{2}=AB^{2}+AC^{2}-2(AB)(AC)\\cos\\angle BAC$ …… 1 mark\n    $=8^{2}+5^{2}-2(8)(5)\\cos 60^{\\circ}=64+25-40=49$ …… 1 mark\n    $BC=7\\text{ cm}$ …… 1 mark\n(b) Area $=\\dfrac{1}{2}(AB)(AC)\\sin\\angle BAC=\\dfrac{1}{2}(8)(5)\\sin 60^{\\circ}$ …… 1 mark\n    $=20\\times\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=10\\sqrt{3}\\text{ cm}^{2}$ …… 1 mark\n(c) Let the required distance be $h$. Taking $BC$ as the base: $\\dfrac{1}{2}(7)h=10\\sqrt{3}$ …… 1 mark\n    $h=\\dfrac{20\\sqrt{3}}{7}\\approx 4.95\\text{ cm}$ …… 1 mark",
    "suggestedMinutes": 9
