    "content": "〔卷一・甲部(2)〕（6 分）\n\n一個袋中有 $5$ 個紅球及 $3$ 個藍球。從袋中隨機抽出兩個球，抽出後不放回。\n(a) 求兩球皆為紅球的概率。（2 分）\n(b) 求兩球一紅一藍的概率。（2 分）\n(c) 求至少抽得一個藍球的概率。（2 分）",
    "explanation": "三問各示範一種標準手法。(a) 不放回，故第二次抽取時分母與分子皆減一。(b) 最常見的失分是漏了乘 2 —— 「一紅一藍」並未指定次序，兩種次序都要計算在內。(c) 示範餘事件：凡見「至少」二字，先想它的反面是甚麼；本題反面只有一種情況（兩紅），比直接列舉「一藍」與「兩藍」快得多，亦更少出錯。",
    "referenceAnswer": "(a) $\\dfrac{5}{14}$\n(b) $\\dfrac{15}{28}$\n(c) $\\dfrac{9}{14}$",
    "marks": 6,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) $\\dfrac{5}{14}$\n(b) $\\dfrac{15}{28}$\n(c) $\\dfrac{9}{14}$",
    "contentEn": "[Paper 1 · Section A(2)] (6 marks)\n\nA bag contains $5$ red balls and $3$ blue balls. Two balls are drawn at random from the bag without replacement.\n(a) Find the probability that both balls are red. (2 marks)\n(b) Find the probability that one ball is red and the other is blue. (2 marks)\n(c) Find the probability that at least one blue ball is drawn. (2 marks)",
    "explanationEn": "Each part demonstrates one standard technique. In (a) there is no replacement, so both the numerator and the denominator fall by one on the second draw. In (b) the commonest loss of marks is omitting the factor 2: \"one red and one blue\" does not specify an order, and both orders must be counted. Part (c) demonstrates the complementary event: whenever the words \"at least\" appear, consider what the opposite is. Here the opposite is a single case (both red), which is quicker and less error-prone than listing \"one blue\" and \"two blue\" separately.",
    "markingScheme": "(a) $P(\\text{兩紅})=\\dfrac{5}{8}\\times\\dfrac{4}{7}$ …… 1 分\n　　$=\\dfrac{20}{56}=\\dfrac{5}{14}$ …… 1 分\n(b) 一紅一藍有兩種次序（先紅後藍、先藍後紅）…… 1 分\n　　$P=2\\times\\dfrac{5}{8}\\times\\dfrac{3}{7}=\\dfrac{30}{56}=\\dfrac{15}{28}$ …… 1 分\n(c) 「至少一藍」的餘事件為「兩球皆紅」…… 1 分\n　　$P=1-\\dfrac{5}{14}=\\dfrac{9}{14}$ …… 1 分",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) $P(\\text{both red})=\\dfrac{5}{8}\\times\\dfrac{4}{7}$ …… 1 mark\n    $=\\dfrac{20}{56}=\\dfrac{5}{14}$ …… 1 mark\n(b) One red and one blue can occur in two orders (red then blue, blue then red) …… 1 mark\n    $P=2\\times\\dfrac{5}{8}\\times\\dfrac{3}{7}=\\dfrac{30}{56}=\\dfrac{15}{28}$ …… 1 mark\n(c) The complementary event of \"at least one blue\" is \"both red\" …… 1 mark\n    $P=1-\\dfrac{5}{14}=\\dfrac{9}{14}$ …… 1 mark",
    "suggestedMinutes": 7
