    "content": "〔卷一・甲部(2)〕（7 分）\n\n已知 $z$ 與 $x$ 成正變，並與 $y$ 的平方成反變。當 $x=4$、$y=3$ 時，$z=8$。\n(a) 以 $x$ 及 $y$ 表示 $z$。（3 分）\n(b) 求當 $x=9$、$y=2$ 時 $z$ 的值。（2 分）\n(c) 若 $x$ 增加 $25\\%$ 而 $y$ 減少 $20\\%$，求 $z$ 的百分變化，答案準確至三位有效數字。（2 分）",
    "explanation": "(c) 是本題的分水嶺。正確做法是把新的 $x$、$y$ 直接代入關係式，讓兩個百分變化各按其冪次作用 —— $x$ 是一次方，故乘 $1.25$；$y$ 是二次方，故除以 $0.8^{2}=0.64$，而非除以 $0.8$。學生最常見的錯，是把 $y$ 減少 $20\\%$ 直接讀成「$z$ 增加 $20\\%$」，忽略了平方。凡遇百分變化題，寫低 $(1+p)$ 與冪次再計算，比心算穩妥。",
    "referenceAnswer": "(a) $z=\\dfrac{18x}{y^{2}}$\n(b) $z=40.5$\n(c) 增加約 $95.3\\%$",
    "marks": 7,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) $z=\\dfrac{18x}{y^{2}}$\n(b) $z=40.5$\n(c) An increase of about $95.3\\%$",
    "contentEn": "[Paper 1 · Section A(2)] (7 marks)\n\nIt is given that $z$ varies directly as $x$ and inversely as the square of $y$. When $x=4$ and $y=3$, $z=8$.\n(a) Express $z$ in terms of $x$ and $y$. (3 marks)\n(b) Find the value of $z$ when $x=9$ and $y=2$. (2 marks)\n(c) If $x$ is increased by $25\\%$ and $y$ is decreased by $20\\%$, find the percentage change in $z$, correct to 3 significant figures. (2 marks)",
    "explanationEn": "Part (c) separates the candidates. The correct method is to substitute the new $x$ and $y$ into the relation and let each percentage change act through its own power: $x$ appears to the first power, so multiply by $1.25$; $y$ appears squared, so divide by $0.8^{2}=0.64$ and not by $0.8$. The commonest error is to read a $20\\%$ decrease in $y$ as a $20\\%$ increase in $z$, ignoring the square. In any percentage-change question, writing down $(1+p)$ together with its power before calculating is safer than working mentally.",
    "markingScheme": "(a) 設 $z=\\dfrac{kx}{y^{2}}$，其中 $k$ 為非零常數 …… 1 分\n　　代入 $x=4,\\ y=3,\\ z=8$：$8=\\dfrac{4k}{9}$ …… 1 分\n　　$k=18$，故 $z=\\dfrac{18x}{y^{2}}$ …… 1 分\n(b) $z=\\dfrac{18(9)}{2^{2}}=\\dfrac{162}{4}$ …… 1 分\n　　$=40.5$ …… 1 分\n(c) 新值 $z'=\\dfrac{18(1.25x)}{(0.8y)^{2}}=\\dfrac{1.25}{0.64}\\times\\dfrac{18x}{y^{2}}=1.953125\\,z$ …… 1 分\n　　百分變化 $=(1.953125-1)\\times100\\%\\approx +95.3\\%$（增加）…… 1 分",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) Let $z=\\dfrac{kx}{y^{2}}$, where $k$ is a non-zero constant …… 1 mark\n    Substitute $x=4,\\ y=3,\\ z=8$: $8=\\dfrac{4k}{9}$ …… 1 mark\n    $k=18$, so $z=\\dfrac{18x}{y^{2}}$ …… 1 mark\n(b) $z=\\dfrac{18(9)}{2^{2}}=\\dfrac{162}{4}$ …… 1 mark\n    $=40.5$ …… 1 mark\n(c) New value $z'=\\dfrac{18(1.25x)}{(0.8y)^{2}}=\\dfrac{1.25}{0.64}\\times\\dfrac{18x}{y^{2}}=1.953125\\,z$ …… 1 mark\n    Percentage change $=(1.953125-1)\\times100\\%\\approx +95.3\\%$ (an increase) …… 1 mark",
    "suggestedMinutes": 9
