    "content": "〔卷一・甲部(2)〕（7 分）\n\n在直角坐標平面上，$A=(-1,\\ 2)$，$B=(5,\\ 6)$。\n(a) 求 $AB$ 的中點 $M$ 的坐標。（1 分）\n(b) 求 $AB$ 的垂直平分線的方程。（3 分）\n(c) 求以 $AB$ 為直徑的圓的方程。（3 分）",
    "explanation": "(c) 有一個容易出錯的位置：$AB$ 是【直徑】而不是半徑，故 $r=\\dfrac{AB}{2}$，而 $r^{2}=\\dfrac{52}{4}=13$。學生常直接把 $AB^{2}=52$ 當作 $r^{2}$，令圓大了一倍。另一個穩妥的做法是用直徑端點式 $(x-x_{1})(x-x_{2})+(y-y_{1})(y-y_{2})=0$ —— 代入 $A$、$B$ 兩點即得同一結果，可作驗算。",
    "referenceAnswer": "(a) $M=(2,\\ 4)$\n(b) $3x+2y-14=0$\n(c) $x^{2}+y^{2}-4x-8y+7=0$",
    "marks": 7,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) $M=(2,\\ 4)$\n(b) $3x+2y-14=0$\n(c) $x^{2}+y^{2}-4x-8y+7=0$",
    "contentEn": "[Paper 1 · Section A(2)] (7 marks)\n\nIn the rectangular coordinate plane, $A=(-1,\\ 2)$ and $B=(5,\\ 6)$.\n(a) Find the coordinates of $M$, the mid-point of $AB$. (1 mark)\n(b) Find the equation of the perpendicular bisector of $AB$. (3 marks)\n(c) Find the equation of the circle with $AB$ as a diameter. (3 marks)",
    "explanationEn": "There is one easy slip in (c): $AB$ is the diameter and not the radius, so $r=\\dfrac{AB}{2}$ and $r^{2}=\\dfrac{52}{4}=13$. Candidates frequently take $AB^{2}=52$ as $r^{2}$, which makes the circle twice the size it should be. A safe alternative is the diameter form $(x-x_{1})(x-x_{2})+(y-y_{1})(y-y_{2})=0$: substituting $A$ and $B$ gives the same equation and serves as a check.",
    "markingScheme": "(a) $M=\\left(\\dfrac{-1+5}{2},\\ \\dfrac{2+6}{2}\\right)=(2,\\ 4)$ …… 1 分\n(b) $AB$ 的斜率 $=\\dfrac{6-2}{5-(-1)}=\\dfrac{4}{6}=\\dfrac{2}{3}$ …… 1 分\n　　垂直平分線的斜率 $=-\\dfrac{3}{2}$（兩垂線斜率之積為 $-1$）…… 1 分\n　　過 $M(2,4)$：$y-4=-\\dfrac{3}{2}(x-2)$，即 $3x+2y-14=0$ …… 1 分\n(c) 圓心為 $M(2,4)$；$AB=\\sqrt{6^{2}+4^{2}}=\\sqrt{52}$，故半徑 $r=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{52}}{2}=\\sqrt{13}$ …… 1 分\n　　$(x-2)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=13$ …… 1 分\n　　展開：$x^{2}+y^{2}-4x-8y+7=0$ …… 1 分",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) $M=\\left(\\dfrac{-1+5}{2},\\ \\dfrac{2+6}{2}\\right)=(2,\\ 4)$ …… 1 mark\n(b) Slope of $AB=\\dfrac{6-2}{5-(-1)}=\\dfrac{4}{6}=\\dfrac{2}{3}$ …… 1 mark\n    Slope of the perpendicular bisector $=-\\dfrac{3}{2}$ (the product of the slopes of perpendicular lines is $-1$) …… 1 mark\n    Through $M(2,4)$: $y-4=-\\dfrac{3}{2}(x-2)$, that is $3x+2y-14=0$ …… 1 mark\n(c) The centre is $M(2,4)$; $AB=\\sqrt{6^{2}+4^{2}}=\\sqrt{52}$, so the radius $r=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{52}}{2}=\\sqrt{13}$ …… 1 mark\n    $(x-2)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=13$ …… 1 mark\n    Expanding: $x^{2}+y^{2}-4x-8y+7=0$ …… 1 mark",
