    "content": "〔卷一・乙部〕（8 分）\n\n設 $f(x)=x^{2}-2kx+(k^{2}+k-6)$，其中 $k$ 為實數。\n(a) 以 $k$ 表示 $f(x)$ 的最小值。（3 分）\n(b) 若方程 $f(x)=0$ 有兩個不相等的實根，求 $k$ 的取值範圍。（3 分）\n(c) 若 $f(x)$ 的最小值為 $-2$，求 $k$ 的值。（2 分）",
    "explanation": "(a) 與 (b) 表面上是兩條不同的路，實際指向同一件事：拋物線開口向上時，「有兩個不相等實根」等價於「最小值小於零」。由 (a) 得最小值為 $k-6$，$k-6<0$ 即 $k<6$，與 (b) 用判別式所得完全一致。做完 (b) 之後用 (a) 的結果驗一次，是零成本的自我檢查。另須留意配方時 $k^{2}$ 已在原式之中，不必額外加減 —— 這正是本題把常數項寫成 $k^{2}+k-6$ 的用意。",
    "referenceAnswer": "(a) 最小值 $=k-6$\n(b) $k<6$\n(c) $k=4$",
    "marks": 8,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) Minimum value $=k-6$\n(b) $k<6$\n(c) $k=4$",
    "contentEn": "[Paper 1 · Section B] (8 marks)\n\nLet $f(x)=x^{2}-2kx+(k^{2}+k-6)$, where $k$ is a real number.\n(a) Express the minimum value of $f(x)$ in terms of $k$. (3 marks)\n(b) If the equation $f(x)=0$ has two distinct real roots, find the range of values of $k$. (3 marks)\n(c) If the minimum value of $f(x)$ is $-2$, find the value of $k$. (2 marks)",
    "explanationEn": "Parts (a) and (b) look like two different routes but point to the same fact: for a parabola opening upwards, \"two distinct real roots\" is equivalent to \"the minimum value is less than zero\". From (a) the minimum is $k-6$, and $k-6<0$ gives $k<6$, exactly as the discriminant does in (b). Checking (b) against the result of (a) is a self-check that costs nothing. Note also that when completing the square the term $k^{2}$ is already present in the expression, so nothing needs to be added and subtracted; that is why the constant term was written as $k^{2}+k-6$.",
    "markingScheme": "(a) 配方：$f(x)=x^{2}-2kx+k^{2}+(k-6)$ …… 1 分\n　　$=(x-k)^{2}+(k-6)$ …… 1 分\n　　由於 $(x-k)^{2}\\geq 0$，最小值為 $k-6$（於 $x=k$ 時取得）…… 1 分\n(b) 判別式 $\\Delta=(-2k)^{2}-4(1)(k^{2}+k-6)$ …… 1 分\n　　$=4k^{2}-4k^{2}-4k+24=-4k+24$ …… 1 分\n　　兩個不相等實根需 $\\Delta>0$：$-4k+24>0 \\Rightarrow k<6$ …… 1 分\n(c) 由 (a)：$k-6=-2$ …… 1 分\n　　$k=4$ …… 1 分",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) Complete the square: $f(x)=x^{2}-2kx+k^{2}+(k-6)$ …… 1 mark\n    $=(x-k)^{2}+(k-6)$ …… 1 mark\n    Since $(x-k)^{2}\\geq 0$, the minimum value is $k-6$, attained at $x=k$ …… 1 mark\n(b) Discriminant $\\Delta=(-2k)^{2}-4(1)(k^{2}+k-6)$ …… 1 mark\n    $=4k^{2}-4k^{2}-4k+24=-4k+24$ …… 1 mark\n    Two distinct real roots require $\\Delta>0$: $-4k+24>0 \\Rightarrow k<6$ …… 1 mark\n(c) From (a): $k-6=-2$ …… 1 mark\n    $k=4$ …… 1 mark",
    "suggestedMinutes": 11
