    "year": 0,
    "content": "〔卷一・乙部〕（8 分）\n\n(a) 解方程 $\\log_{3}x+\\log_{3}(x-2)=1$。（4 分）\n(b) 解方程 $2^{2x}-5(2^{x})+4=0$。（4 分）",
    "explanation": "兩問各有一個必須做的動作。(a) 必須【檢驗根】：合併對數的步驟會擴大定義域，因此解出的根未必全部合法，$x=-1$ 令 $\\log_{3}x$ 無定義，須明確寫出「捨去」及理由 —— 只寫 $x=3$ 而不交代為何棄掉另一根，步驟分會被扣。(b) 必須【看出 $2^{2x}=(2^{x})^{2}$】，這是換元的入口；換元後亦應註明 $u>0$，因為指數函數恆正 —— 本題兩個根碰巧都是正數，但若題目改動係數而出現負根，這一句就是取捨的依據。",
    "referenceAnswer": "(a) $x=3$\n(b) $x=0$ 或 $x=2$",
    "marks": 8,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) $x=3$\n(b) $x=0$ or $x=2$",
    "contentEn": "[Paper 1 · Section B] (8 marks)\n\n(a) Solve the equation $\\log_{3}x+\\log_{3}(x-2)=1$. (4 marks)\n(b) Solve the equation $2^{2x}-5(2^{x})+4=0$. (4 marks)",
    "explanationEn": "Each part has one step that must be performed. In (a) the roots must be checked: combining logarithms widens the domain, so not every root obtained is admissible. Here $x=-1$ makes $\\log_{3}x$ undefined and must be rejected with the reason stated; writing $x=3$ alone, without saying why the other root was discarded, loses step marks. In (b) the entry point is seeing that $2^{2x}=(2^{x})^{2}$, which allows the substitution; the condition $u>0$ should also be stated, since an exponential is always positive. Both roots happen to be positive here, but if the coefficients were changed so that a negative root appeared, that condition would be what rejects it.",
    "markingScheme": "(a) 合併對數：$\\log_{3}[x(x-2)]=1$ …… 1 分\n　　化為指數式：$x(x-2)=3^{1}=3$ …… 1 分\n　　$x^{2}-2x-3=0 \\Rightarrow (x-3)(x+1)=0$，得 $x=3$ 或 $x=-1$ …… 1 分\n　　檢驗：$x=-1$ 時 $\\log_{3}(-1)$ 無定義，須捨去。故 $x=3$ …… 1 分\n(b) 留意 $2^{2x}=(2^{x})^{2}$。設 $u=2^{x}$（$u>0$）…… 1 分\n　　方程化為 $u^{2}-5u+4=0$ …… 1 分\n　　$(u-1)(u-4)=0$，得 $u=1$ 或 $u=4$ …… 1 分\n　　$2^{x}=1 \\Rightarrow x=0$；$2^{x}=4 \\Rightarrow x=2$ …… 1 分",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) Combine the logarithms: $\\log_{3}[x(x-2)]=1$ …… 1 mark\n    Convert to index form: $x(x-2)=3^{1}=3$ …… 1 mark\n    $x^{2}-2x-3=0 \\Rightarrow (x-3)(x+1)=0$, giving $x=3$ or $x=-1$ …… 1 mark\n    Check: $\\log_{3}(-1)$ is undefined when $x=-1$, so it must be rejected. Hence $x=3$ …… 1 mark\n(b) Note that $2^{2x}=(2^{x})^{2}$. Let $u=2^{x}$, where $u>0$ …… 1 mark\n    The equation becomes $u^{2}-5u+4=0$ …… 1 mark\n    $(u-1)(u-4)=0$, giving $u=1$ or $u=4$ …… 1 mark\n    $2^{x}=1 \\Rightarrow x=0$; $2^{x}=4 \\Rightarrow x=2$ …… 1 mark",
    "suggestedMinutes": 11
