    "content": "〔卷一・乙部〕（8 分）\n\n一等比數列的首項為 $3$，公比為 $2$。\n(a) 求該數列的第 $8$ 項。（2 分）\n(b) 求該數列首 $n$ 項之和 $S_{n}$，答案以 $n$ 表示。（3 分）\n(c) 求最小的正整數 $n$，使 $S_{n}>5000$。（3 分）",
    "explanation": "(c) 與第 10 題的「求最小 $n$」同屬一類，同樣必須驗證兩端：$n=10$ 不成立、$n=11$ 成立。分別在於等比數列的 $S_{n}$ 含 $2^{n}$，增長極快，試值只需一兩步即可收窄，反而比取對數更快更可靠。若選擇取對數，須留意 $\\log$ 兩邊同底且不等號方向不變（底數大於 1），並且最後仍要取整數並回代驗證。",
    "referenceAnswer": "(a) $T_{8}=384$\n(b) $S_{n}=3(2^{n}-1)$\n(c) $n=11$",
    "marks": 8,
    "referenceAnswerEn": "(a) $T_{8}=384$\n(b) $S_{n}=3(2^{n}-1)$\n(c) $n=11$",
    "contentEn": "[Paper 1 · Section B] (8 marks)\n\nThe first term of a geometric sequence is $3$ and the common ratio is $2$.\n(a) Find the 8th term of the sequence. (2 marks)\n(b) Find $S_{n}$, the sum of the first $n$ terms, in terms of $n$. (3 marks)\n(c) Find the least positive integer $n$ such that $S_{n}>5000$. (3 marks)",
    "explanationEn": "Part (c) belongs to the same \"least $n$\" family as question 10, and again both ends must be verified: $n=10$ fails and $n=11$ succeeds. The difference is that $S_{n}$ for a geometric sequence contains $2^{n}$ and grows very fast, so trying values narrows the answer in one or two steps and is quicker and more reliable than taking logarithms. If logarithms are used, both sides must be taken to the same base with the inequality unchanged in direction (the base exceeds 1), and the answer must still be rounded to an integer and substituted back to verify.",
    "markingScheme": "(a) $T_{n}=ar^{n-1}$，故 $T_{8}=3\\times2^{7}$ …… 1 分\n　　$=384$ …… 1 分\n(b) $S_{n}=\\dfrac{a(r^{n}-1)}{r-1}=\\dfrac{3(2^{n}-1)}{2-1}$ …… 2 分\n　　$=3(2^{n}-1)$ …… 1 分\n(c) 需 $3(2^{n}-1)>5000$，即 $2^{n}>\\dfrac{5000}{3}+1\\approx1667.7$ …… 1 分\n　　當 $n=10$：$S_{10}=3(1024-1)=3069<5000$ …… 1 分\n　　當 $n=11$：$S_{11}=3(2048-1)=6141>5000$，故最小的 $n$ 為 $11$ …… 1 分",
    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) $T_{n}=ar^{n-1}$, so $T_{8}=3\\times2^{7}$ …… 1 mark\n    $=384$ …… 1 mark\n(b) $S_{n}=\\dfrac{a(r^{n}-1)}{r-1}=\\dfrac{3(2^{n}-1)}{2-1}$ …… 2 marks\n    $=3(2^{n}-1)$ …… 1 mark\n(c) Require $3(2^{n}-1)>5000$, that is $2^{n}>\\dfrac{5000}{3}+1\\approx1667.7$ …… 1 mark\n    When $n=10$: $S_{10}=3(1024-1)=3069<5000$ …… 1 mark\n    When $n=11$: $S_{11}=3(2048-1)=6141>5000$, so the least $n$ is $11$ …… 1 mark",
    "suggestedMinutes": 11
